260
00:17:05,610 --> 00:17:07,220
Oh yeah, Yukiya...

261
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:10,140
I remember you like your stew sweet.

262
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,490
Could you try tasting it?

263
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:13,980
O-Okay.

264
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:16,770
Oh, wait.

265
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:25,000
Hm? What's wrong?

266
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,710
It's okay now.

267
00:17:27,070 --> 00:17:30,920
What's wrong? Are you feeling shy?

268
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:35,210
Or do you want me 
to blow on it some more?

269
00:17:35,210 --> 00:17:37,500
Stop it. You're going to 
get your spit in it.

270
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:50,270
I guess it's on the better side.

271
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:52,850
Right? It's pretty good, right?

272
00:17:52,850 --> 00:17:55,720
<i>This was my absolute favorite flavor.</i>

273
00:17:57,580 --> 00:17:58,980
<i>I knew it.</i>

274
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:01,690
<i>I got him good!</i>

275
00:18:01,690 --> 00:18:03,000
<i>Of course.</i>

276
00:18:03,470 --> 00:18:05,400
<i>Of course!</i>

277
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:08,870
Are you sure?

278
00:18:08,870 --> 00:18:10,460
Don't cut your fingers.

279
00:18:10,910 --> 00:18:13,870
Make a cat paw with your left hand, okay?

280
00:18:13,870 --> 00:18:15,370
You say that like I'm stupid.

281
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:17,430
I know how to use a knife.

282
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:19,230
Oh, wow.

283
00:18:19,230 --> 00:18:20,960
You're doing diagonal cuts.

284
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:25,250
Is it because you're always so salty 
that you know how to cook?

285
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:27,690
In fact, I've been 
making miso soup lately.

286
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:29,130
You? Really?

287
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:31,050
Make me some, then!

288
00:18:31,050 --> 00:18:35,170
Fool. Don't expect any soup for you.

289
00:18:35,170 --> 00:18:38,440
<i>We haven't even started eating and 
it's so sweet I'm getting heartburn.</i>

290
00:18:40,530 --> 00:18:43,240
Wow! You're always such a good cook!

291
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:45,970
Yukiya did help out.

292
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,970
Well, I'll be heading home now.

293
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:51,710
Huh? Aren't you going to eat with us?

294
00:18:52,050 --> 00:18:54,700
Nah, I just came to cook.

295
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:56,210
I'll eat at home.

296
00:18:57,850 --> 00:18:59,140
Stay for dinner.

297
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:05,510
I mean, you'll get lonely having 
dinner with just me, right?

298
00:19:06,710 --> 00:19:08,100
Exactly.

299
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:10,850
Onii looks lonely, too.

300
00:19:12,310 --> 00:19:14,680
You haven't been here 
in such a long time.

301
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:18,180
You should make yourself 
at home, if you don't mind.

302
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:20,000
Okay...

303
00:19:20,730 --> 00:19:24,400
I guess I wouldn't mind, if you insist.

304
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:30,490
I'll let Mom know, though.

305
00:19:30,490 --> 00:19:31,700
Huh?

306
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,620
Mom

307
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,620
Today

308
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,620
Missed Call
              Missed Call
                           Missed Call

309
00:19:35,130 --> 00:19:35,970
Mom?

310
00:19:35,970 --> 00:19:36,930
<i>Miku?</i>

311
00:19:36,930 --> 00:19:39,070
<i>Thank goodness. Are you all right?</i>

312
00:19:39,070 --> 00:19:39,790
Huh?

313
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:42,330
<i>I went home to get something earlier,</i>

314
00:19:42,330 --> 00:19:45,100
<i>and the door was unlocked 
and no one was home.</i>

315
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:47,710
Sorry! I left in such a hurry...

316
00:19:48,530 --> 00:19:50,770
<i>She came here in a hurry?</i>

317
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:20,620
Hey...

318
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:22,220
Sorry about today.

319
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:28,300
Like, I've never seen you 
cooking like a grown-up before.

320
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,820
It took me by surprise.

321
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:33,440
Wakana seemed happy, too.

322
00:20:33,970 --> 00:20:37,260
Plus it was pretty helpful overall.

323
00:20:39,370 --> 00:20:40,660
Thanks.

324
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:52,040
Thanks for walking me home.

325
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,210
Good night.

326
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,740
What's wrong?

327
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,630
Er...

328
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:03,730
I left home in a hurry, and...

329
00:21:05,390 --> 00:21:09,250
I think I left my keys inside.

330
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:14,550
Mom locked the door 
on her way to her night shift.

331
00:21:27,850 --> 00:21:30,190
Th-Then...

332
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:34,320
Wanna stay over?

333
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,050
'Kay.

334
00:23:25,010 --> 00:23:40,170
Next Time
My Childhood Friend Wants to Win

335
00:23:27,330 --> 00:23:28,250
Okay...

336
00:23:28,250 --> 00:23:30,880
If Onii ends up taking it too far,

337
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:35,440
we're going to change the title from
"I Want to End This Love Game," right?

338
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:38,030
Next episode: "My Childhood 
Friend Wants to Win."

